{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0152iuc9guVuhUBWH7ZEVi4w","type":"tool_result","content":"1010:**Review threat model.** A review hunts defects in a normal working\n1011-environment: the content agents write into the repository (the gates exist to\n1012-check it), supported configurations, and regressions of supported behavior.\n1013-A finding whose reproduction needs the host itself compromised or contrived (a\n1014-fake or hostile binary, a shim whose output depends on the working directory,\n1015-the environment or `PATH` changed by another process mid-call, a tampered OS\n1016-or tool) is out of scope: it is dismissed in one recorded line by whoever\n1017-rules the finding, in the response to the review verdict (and in the\n1018-delegated-decisions record too, when the run keeps one), and never answered\n1019-with code. A finding whose reproduction needs a contrived, improbable scenario\n1020-is dismissed the same way (owner ruling 2026-10-13): a hand act the process\n1021-forbids (rewinding the trunk branch, skipping or disabling a hook,\n1022-hand-editing a generated view or a ruled record), or ordinary tools run in an\n1023-order no supported workflow or kit route produces. Severity tracks\n1024-plausibility and impact, not ingenuity, and reachability gates every class: a\n1025-fail-open, data-loss or security path counts only when a supported workflow or\n1026-the kit's own routes reach it; a rare or contrived path is MINOR at most, or\n1027-dismissed as above. Whoever rules a finding re-grades a mislabelled BLOCKER\n1028-or MAJOR. A spec's promise over an input space reaches only what supported\n1029-workflows and the kit's own routes produce: hand-edited kit-written state, a\n1030-hand-chosen name alias (case, trailing dots and the like) and a sub-second\n1031-timing window lie outside it unless the spec names them as inside, so a\n1032-finding that needs one is not stated behaviour. Forge mode's \"bugs and fail-open, not malice\"\n1033-(process-options.md \"Parallel work\") is the same bound.\n1034-\n1035-Keep `status.md` short so a reviewer can orient cheaply — the *whole file* is\n1036-the working surface (§5); the full history lives in `log.md` and need not be\n1037-re-read each pass.\n1038-\n1039-**Model/agent tiering — recommend + record, not enforce.** The risk triage above\n1040-is also a **tiering** axis: planning, decomposition, decisions, and high-risk\n001-ADJUDICATE-9b5ecc2.md\n001-ADJUDICATE-9b5ecc2.md.requested\n001-DISPUTE-findings.toml\nbrief = dispute\nkinds = F1\noutcome = pending","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bf70e8e2-9747-4c15-a988-52ecbf5dfbe0","uuid":"f958caea-e8aa-408f-bdd0-9efcf8de4427","timestamp":"2026-10-18T14:52:04.724Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1010:**Review threat model.** A review hunts defects in a normal working\n1011-environment: the content agents write into the repository (the gates exist to\n1012-check it), supported configurations, and regressions of supported behavior.\n1013-A finding whose reproduction needs the host itself compromised or contrived (a\n1014-fake or hostile binary, a shim whose output depends on the working directory,\n1015-the environment or `PATH` changed by another process mid-call, a tampered OS\n1016-or tool) is out of scope: it is dismissed in one recorded line by whoever\n1017-rules the finding, in the response to the review verdict (and in the\n1018-delegated-decisions record too, when the run keeps one), and never answered\n1019-with code. A finding whose reproduction needs a contrived, improbable scenario\n1020-is dismissed the same way (owner ruling 2026-10-13): a hand act the process\n1021-forbids (rewinding the trunk branch, skipping or disabling a hook,\n1022-hand-editing a generated view or a ruled record), or ordinary tools run in an\n1023-order no supported workflow or kit route produces. Severity tracks\n1024-plausibility and impact, not ingenuity, and reachability gate